/E (This appendix section contains detailed programmatic descriptions and implementation layouts of the custom lexical fortification architecture developed throughout this research project. To provide complete clarity for replication, the primary logic driving the automated text perturbation engine is designed to interface with active Python environments using the Natural Language Toolkit library. The function identifies valid alphabetic strings, shuffles the input candidate array to maintain stochastic variance, and evaluates synset lemmas to locate substitution words.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 301 0 R
/E (The training configurations utilize the Hugging Face training arguments framework to execute a parallelized optimization sequence. By disabling internal checkpoint saving strategies, the system avoids input-output blockages on the cloud platform, allowing maximum throughput for training text matrices. The real-time verification system uses a Gradio web layout to deploy the fine-tuned model weights directly onto accessible web applications. This enables users to evaluate model resilience interactively by comparing the output distributions of the baseline model against the fortified neural network on the fly.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
