/Title (In addition to evaluating text classification accuracy, our research extensively analyzes the computational overhead and operational efficiency of our fortification pipeline to ensure its feasibility in production environments. Traditional adversarial training methods that rely on continuous genetic search loops or combinatorial token optimization require heavy computing power, often adding significant delays that make real-time deployment impossible on standard hardware. Our framework solves this efficiency issue by completely separating the text perturbation engine from the deep transformer backpropagation steps during training. By using a localized NLTK WordNet framework to generate synonyms instantly on the host memory before passing data to the GPU, we minimize data transmission delays between systems. Our experimental logs show that adding the synonym injection layer increases the training time per epoch by only seven point four percent compared to standard clean fine-tuning, which is a major speed improvement over traditional adversarial libraries requiring massive, expensive GPU clusters.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 310 0 R
/First 386 0 R
/Last 386 0 R
/Count -1
>>
